module

-- **Yours (H).** A front-end theorem: what the rule proofs stand on. It arrives
-- as a `sorry` and a signature install leaves it alone.
--
-- **Type preservation** — the SMT side.
--
-- A term the semantics gives a type at all has a *well-formed* type. Without
-- this nothing downstream may assume the types it is handed are ones the model
-- can interpret, and every lemma that inspects a type has to re-establish it.
--
-- Could in principle arrive proven: the statement is about the generated
-- `__smtx_typeof` and `__smtx_type_wf`, which come from `smt.eos` — the same
-- for every calculus over ordinary SMT-LIB. It is left open here only because
-- the template does not yet carry the proof.
--
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- What Logos does here
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- `Cpc/Proofs/TypePreservation/`: **17,691 lines across 16 files**, against
-- CpcMini's 4,234 across 10. Files are organised by theory --
-- `CoreArith.lean`, `BitVec.lean`, `Sets.lean`, `SeqStringRegex.lean` -- which
-- is the clearest evidence that the cost here follows the theories rather than
-- the rules.
--
-- Roughly half of it is invariant between the two packages:
-- `Datatypes.lean` (1,334 lines) is byte-identical, `Common.lean` (529) differs
-- by four lines. The theory-specific halves are where the size lives.
--
-- **Whether it can be inherited depends on your `smt.eos`.** The statement is
-- about definitions generated from the SMT-LIB semantics, so a proof of it
-- transfers only while that semantics is the stock one — which is exactly what
-- the `logos-smt` entry of `install/defs/profile.conf` records. Supply your own
-- `smt.eos`, change what a type is or what a well-formed model is, and this
-- becomes yours no matter what upstream ships.
public import @CALCULUS@.ModelWf
import all @CALCULUS@.ModelWf

@[expose] public section

namespace Smtm

/-- A term the semantics types has a well-formed type. -/
theorem smtx_typeof_wf (s : SmtTerm) :
    __smtx_typeof s ≠ SmtType.None ->
    __smtx_type_wf (__smtx_typeof s) = true := by
  sorry

end Smtm
